---
title: Creating a Registrar Integration
description: Build domain registrar adapters for FOSSBilling.
---

{% partial file="./_breaking-changes-caution.mdoc" /%}

Registrar adapters let FOSSBilling communicate with domain registrars to register, transfer, and manage domains on behalf of your customers.

## File Structure

Place your adapter in:

{% filetree %}
- library/Registrar/Adapter/
  - YourRegistrar.php
{% /filetree %}

Your class must extend `Registrar_AdapterAbstract` and implement its required methods.

## Common Methods

FOSSBilling passes a `Registrar_Domain` to domain operations. See [`Registrar_AdapterAbstract`](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/blob/0.8.9/src/library/Registrar/AdapterAbstract.php) for every required method and its signature.

| Method | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `isDomainAvailable()` | Check domain availability |
| `registerDomain()` | Register a new domain |
| `transferDomain()` | Request a domain transfer |
| `renewDomain()` | Renew a domain |
| `getDomainDetails()` | Read domain details from the registrar |
| `modifyNs()` | Update nameservers |
| `modifyContact()` | Update contact information |

## Namecheap Walkthrough

The bundled Namecheap adapter illustrates availability checks and registration. [Namecheap adapter source](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/blob/0.8.9/src/library/Registrar/Adapter/Namecheap.php)

1. **Configure the registrar.** `getConfig()` defines the admin form and marks the API key as secret. The constructor requires an API key, a username, and the server’s public IP address. [Configuration code](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/blob/0.8.9/src/library/Registrar/Adapter/Namecheap.php#L26-L89)
2. **Check availability.** `isDomainAvailable()` builds the name from the domain object and sends `namecheap.domains.check`. It reads the availability flag and rejects premium domains. [Availability check](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/blob/0.8.9/src/library/Registrar/Adapter/Namecheap.php#L91-L109)
3. **Register the domain.** `registerDomain()` sends the name, registration period, contacts, and any configured nameservers. It returns `true` when Namecheap confirms the registration. [Registration code](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/blob/0.8.9/src/library/Registrar/Adapter/Namecheap.php#L421-L506)
4. **Handle provider errors.** Both operations use `_makeRequest()` to add authentication and parse the XML response. The helper raises `Registrar_Exception` for provider-reported error statuses. [Request handling](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/blob/0.8.9/src/library/Registrar/Adapter/Namecheap.php#L121-L169)

## Testing Your Adapter

{% steps %}
1. Create a test domain product in FOSSBilling
2. Configure your registrar adapter in **System → Domain Registration**
3. Test domain availability checks
4. Test registration (if possible with registrar's test environment)
5. Verify contact information syncing
{% /steps %}

